meta {
  name: 99 Notification Test Flow
  seq: 99
}

docs {
  # Notification Test Flow

  End-to-end automation for the patient notification templates. Run the
  requests top-to-bottom (they capture ids into env vars as they go):

    Auth → Create global templates (Site Admin) → Enable/clone for the
    business (priya) → Enable channels → Create test data → Trigger the 5
    events → Verify the resolved notifications.

  ## Select the environment
  Pick the **NotificationTest** environment before running, and set the two
  secret vars (never stored in the collection):
    - BUSINESS_PASSWORD   → password for priya@email.com
    - SITEADMIN_PASSWORD  → Site Admin password (seeded default: SuperSecret1)

  ## What it creates
  One diagnostic EMAIL template per feature, whose body prints EVERY supported
  placeholder as `label: {tag}` so you can confirm each one resolves:

    - lab_create_order_inform_patient            (Lab Create Order)
    - lab_order_report_published_inform_patient  (Lab Report Completed / Published)
    - lab_order_completed_inform_patient         (Lab Order Completed)
    - complete_payment_for_lab_order_inform_patient
    - partial_payment_for_lab_order_inform_patient

  EMAIL is used because the resolved body is stored verbatim on the
  CommunicationLog row (viewable in "50 Verify — Communications") even if the
  outbound Exchange gateway is not configured. To also test WhatsApp, duplicate
  the "Create Global" requests with `preference: WHATSAPP` plus `templateType`
  and `templateCategory` (WhatsApp renders params positionally, so it is harder
  to eyeball — EMAIL is the clean verification path).

  ## Triggers
    1. Create Order        → POST /orders (status ORDER)      → lab_create_order
    2. Partial Payment     → POST /payments (part of balance)  → partial_payment
    3. Complete Payment    → POST /payments (clears balance)   → complete_payment
    4. Publish Lab Report  → POST /lab-reports/:id/publish      → report published
    5. Complete Order      → publish ALL reports on the order   → order completed

  Scenarios 4 & 5 need an order with REAL catalogue lab tests whose reports have
  been taken through the reporting workflow to at least APPROVED. The free-text
  "direct" order created here has no reports, so those two requests include
  discovery + notes (see their docs).

  ## IMPORTANT — template precedence (read this)
  Delivery resolves the most-specific ACTIVE template, in order:
      (1) tenant + branch   →   (2) tenant + null (tenant-level)   →   (3) global
  and the notification dispatch passes a branch for some events but NOT others:
      - order.created, lab-report.published, order.completed → dispatch WITH the
        event's branch, so a BRANCH-LEVEL template (the clone from requests
        20-24, created in priya's active branch) WINS.
      - payment.received (partial & complete) → dispatch with branch = null, so
        only tenant-level / global templates are considered.

  Consequence on a tenant that ALREADY has its own templates (priya's does — it
  has tenant-level, isDefault templates for every feature/channel):
      - Create Order / Report Published / Order Completed → the branch clone
        wins → your tag body renders.  ✅
      - Partial / Complete Payment → resolve tenant-wide to the tenant's
        EXISTING tenant-level template, which the SITE_ADMIN global cannot beat.
        priya only has branch-level (doctor) profiles, so she CANNOT edit the
        tenant-level payment templates.  ⚠️

  On a FRESH tenant (no own templates) all five resolve straight from the
  SITE_ADMIN globals — nothing shadows them. ✅

  ### To render the tag body for the 2 payment events on an existing tenant
  Sign in as a BUSINESS_ADMIN (a tenant-level, branch = null profile) of that
  tenant and either:
    a) PATCH the tenant-level partial/complete payment templates' `template`
       field to the diagnostic body (GET /templates?preference=EMAIL then
       PATCH /templates/:id), or
    b) create tenant-level templates (POST /templates from a business_admin
       session so branchId is null) with isDefault=true.
  A branch-scoped session (like priya's) cannot do either — findById/list scope
  by the caller's branch, and payment dispatch ignores branch templates.

  ## Verifying (works even with no live gateway)
  Each triggered event writes a CommunicationLog row PER channel with the
  RESOLVED body already substituted (EMAIL) or positional templateParams
  (WhatsApp) — inspect them in "50 Verify - Communications". The outbound
  Exchange gateway does not need to be configured to verify tag resolution.
}
